statement:
Let P ∈ ℕ, let μ be a measure on the Borel σ-algebra of ℝ^P, and let g : ℝ^P → ℝ and θ ∈ ℝ. Let t ⊆ ℝ^P be a countable set and B : ℝ^P → 𝒫(ℝ^P) a family of sets, and put V := ⋃_{x∈t} B(x). Assume:
- B(x) is measurable for every x ∈ t;
- the sets B(x), x ∈ t, are pairwise disjoint, i.e. B(x) ∩ B(y) = ∅ for distinct x, y ∈ t;
- μ(V) < ∞;
- g is μ-integrable on V.
If ∫_{B(x)} g dμ ≤ θ·μ(B(x)) for every x ∈ t, then ∫_V g dμ ≤ θ·μ(V). All measures are read as real numbers via ENNReal.toReal.
